&lt;p&gt;The Role&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Lead Data Platform Engineer to provide hands-on technical leadership in designing, building and evolving secure, scalable and reliable data platforms for clients across the public sector and utilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work across cloud-native and distributed data platforms, helping engineering teams build reliable platform capabilities that support batch, real-time streaming, analytical and operational workloads.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role combines hands-on engineering with technical leadership. You will contribute to platform architecture and design decisions, establish engineering standards, solve complex technical challenges and work closely with architects, engineers and client stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong experience with cloud platforms, distributed systems and data platform engineering is essential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the design, development and evolution of secure, scalable data platform services and components.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement platform capabilities supporting batch, real-time streaming and hybrid workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and optimise distributed data services using technologies such as Kafka, Kinesis, Spark, Flink or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to platform architecture and technical design decisions, balancing scalability, security, performance and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with architects and engineers to establish reusable platform patterns, standards and engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop cloud-native data platform capabilities using AWS and/or Azure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support high availability, fault tolerance, resilience and low-latency performance across platform services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and maintain approaches to data modelling, schema management, data quality and data integrity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive engineering best practices including CI/CD, automated testing, TDD, observability and Infrastructure as Code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support platform monitoring, troubleshooting, performance optimisation and root cause analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to resilience, disaster recovery and operational readiness activities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with DevOps and Platform Engineering teams to improve deployment and operational processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support technical discovery and solution design with client stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance, mentoring and support to Senior Data and Platform Engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical risks, dependencies and opportunities for continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Essential Technical Skills &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial experience in Data Platform Engineering, Data Engineering, Software Engineering or a similar technical discipline, with experience operating at Lead level.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and building cloud-native, distributed data platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with Java and/or Python or equivalent modern programming languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with streaming and event-driven architectures, including Kafka, Kinesis or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with large-scale data processing technologies such as Spark, Flink, Kafka Streams or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience working with AWS and/or Azure cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS services such as S3, Lambda, Glue, RDS, Athena, EC2 and IAM is desirable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data pipeline architecture, orchestration and optimisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with relational and NoSQL databases, including data modelling and performance tuning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing CI/CD, automated testing, observability and platform reliability practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of DevOps and Infrastructure as Code.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with GitHub/GitLab or equivalent source control platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in Agile and/or DevOps environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desirable: Terraform, Docker, Kubernetes, Ansible, Packer, Elasticsearch/OpenSearch, Jenkins, GitLab CI, Python, Bash or Linux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working within public sector, utilities or other regulated environments is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Technical Leadership&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Lead Data Platform Engineer, you will provide technical leadership within delivery teams and platform engineering activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the technical delivery of data platform capabilities and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to platform architecture, technical design and technology decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish reusable engineering patterns and promote consistent technical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support and mentor Senior Data and Platform Engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with architects, developers, DevOps and client stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify technical debt, platform risks and opportunities for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote secure, scalable, observable and maintainable engineering practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support teams in balancing technical quality with delivery timelines and client outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to platform resilience, operational readiness and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience &amp;amp; Qualifications&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent experience in Computer Science, Software Engineering, Data Engineering or a related technical discipline is desirable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should have 5+ years of relevant professional experience across Data Engineering, Software Engineering, Platform Engineering or a similar technical discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For a Lead-level appointment, you should demonstrate experience taking ownership of complex platform engineering solutions, technical decisions and mentoring or guiding other engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Security Clearance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Where required by the client assignment, UK Government Security Check (SC) clearance may be required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Candidates who do not currently hold SC clearance may be supported through the clearance process, subject to eligibility requirements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;About You&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a hands-on platform engineer who understands how to build reliable data infrastructure that works in production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You enjoy solving complex problems across cloud, distributed systems, streaming, data platforms and infrastructure, and can translate architectural requirements into practical engineering solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are comfortable moving between hands-on development, technical design and stakeholder discussions, while helping other engineers improve their technical capability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You care about reliability, scalability, security, observability and maintainability, not simply getting a platform into production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working within public sector, utilities or other complex and regulated environments would be highly advantageous.&lt;/p&gt;
